From: Kristianaaron <25537000+Kristianaaron@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zink: make VK_KHR_maintenance5 optional

Zink requires VK_KHR_maintenance5, which Vulkan 1.3 drivers that predate it
(NVIDIA's Tegra R36 driver, 540 branch, Vulkan 1.3.251, on Tegra X1 / GM20B)
do not expose; Zink then fails in feature detection, silently in release
builds.

Zink depends on it in three places only:
- the point-size property polygonModePointSize, already handled when false;
- deleting PointSize stores relies on "a default size of 1.0 is used if
  PointSize is not written": keep the store when maintenance5 is absent;
- VkBufferUsageFlags2CreateInfo on buffer views: chain it only with
  maintenance5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_compiler.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_compiler.c
@@ -3055,8 +3055,11 @@
    if (var) {
       bool can_remove = false;
       if (!nir_find_variable_with_location(consumer, nir_var_shader_in, VARYING_SLOT_PSIZ)) {
-         /* maintenance5 guarantees "A default size of 1.0 is used if PointSize is not written" */
-         if (!var->data.explicit_xfb_buffer && delete_psiz_store(producer, true))
+         /* maintenance5 guarantees "A default size of 1.0 is used if PointSize is not written";
+          * without it the write must stay.
+          */
+         if (screen->info.have_KHR_maintenance5 &&
+             !var->data.explicit_xfb_buffer && delete_psiz_store(producer, true))
             can_remove = !(producer->info.outputs_written & VARYING_BIT_PSIZ);
          else if (consumer->info.stage != MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT)
             can_remove = !var->data.explicit_location;
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
@@ -1007,7 +1007,9 @@
          NULL,
          VK_BUFFER_USAGE_UNIFORM_TEXEL_BUFFER_BIT
       };
-      bvci.pNext = &usage;
+      /* VkBufferUsageFlags2CreateInfo is a maintenance5 structure */
+      if (screen->info.have_KHR_maintenance5)
+         bvci.pNext = &usage;
       if (zink_get_format_props(screen, format)->bufferFeatures & VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_STORAGE_TEXEL_BUFFER_BIT)
          usage.usage |= VK_BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE_TEXEL_BUFFER_BIT;
 
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_device_info.py
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_device_info.py
@@ -68,8 +68,7 @@
               features=True),
     Extension("VK_KHR_maintenance5",
               alias="maint5",
-              features=True, properties=True,
-              required=True),
+              features=True, properties=True),
     Extension("VK_KHR_maintenance6",
               alias="maint6",
               features=True, properties=True),
